1
00:00:00,257 --> 00:00:04,587
Atlantic Technology signs our fictional one hundred fifty thousand dollar

2
00:00:04,587 --> 00:00:05,260
agreement.

3
00:00:05,580 --> 00:00:06,910
Michael celebrates.

4
00:00:07,216 --> 00:00:10,760
That signature creates a commercial commitment, but it does not

5
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:14,355
tell us what has been invoiced, collected, or earned under

6
00:00:14,355 --> 00:00:15,363
accounting rules.

7
00:00:16,423 --> 00:00:20,521
A booking records a qualifying commercial commitment under the organization’s

8
00:00:20,521 --> 00:00:21,696
reporting policy.

9
00:00:22,016 --> 00:00:24,918
An invoice requests payment under the terms.

10
00:00:25,250 --> 00:00:28,397
Cash collection records money actually received.

11
00:00:28,717 --> 00:00:33,820
Recognized revenue follows satisfaction of obligations under the applicable accounting

12
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:34,428
rules.

13
00:00:35,492 --> 00:00:40,058
For teaching, assume this campaign’s services qualify for equal recognition

14
00:00:40,058 --> 00:00:41,362
over three months.

15
00:00:41,652 --> 00:00:45,227
The illustration allocates fifty thousand dollars to each month.

16
00:00:45,555 --> 00:00:49,981
Actual recognition can differ with the deliverables, service periods, contract

17
00:00:49,981 --> 00:00:52,064
structure, and accounting policy.

18
00:00:53,106 --> 00:00:57,578
The customer might pay before delivery, in installments, or later

19
00:00:57,578 --> 00:00:58,560
under the agreement.

20
00:00:58,879 --> 00:01:02,488
The invoice and cash dates can therefore move separately from

21
00:01:02,488 --> 00:01:03,702
the revenue timeline.

22
00:01:04,021 --> 00:01:07,642
A contract’s total value does not describe every clock at

23
00:01:07,642 --> 00:01:08,264
once.

24
00:01:09,319 --> 00:01:12,863
A bookings dashboard can show one hundred fifty thousand while

25
00:01:12,926 --> 00:01:16,626
a monthly revenue report shows fifty thousand under our assumption.

26
00:01:16,962 --> 00:01:19,334
A cash report may show another amount.

27
00:01:19,658 --> 00:01:23,369
Compare the same concepts and periods before calling a difference

28
00:01:23,369 --> 00:01:23,982
an error.

29
00:01:25,026 --> 00:01:30,828
The analyst supports definitions, mappings, reconciliations, and approved integrations.

30
00:01:31,212 --> 00:01:34,874
Finance determines accounting policy and recognition treatment.

31
00:01:35,194 --> 00:01:40,258
Establishing that boundary helps commercial systems provide trustworthy information without

32
00:01:40,258 --> 00:01:43,869
assigning the analyst responsibilities they do not hold.
